course: dictionary
lesson: 13152
title: Forfeit: losing by rule
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Forfeit has a few related meanings, and the words around it tell you which one you need. «The team had to forfeit the match because they did not turn up» shows the team lost because they did not play.
explain: Forfeit can also be a noun, something you must give up or do as a punishment. «At the party, the loser had to pay a forfeit and do a silly dance.» The clues are party and silly dance, so a forfeit is a task the loser must do in a game.
explain: Forfeit can also mean losing something because you broke a rule. «If you do not pay on time, you forfeit your place.» Try the swap test: put lose in the sentence. «If you do not pay on time, you lose your place» still makes sense, so forfeit means lose here.
fact: Forfeit can be a verb (to forfeit something) or a noun (a forfeit).
fact: «Forfeit» (verb) means to lose something or give it up because you broke a rule or did not do something.
fact: «Forfeit» (sport) means to lose a game because you did not play or broke the rules.
fact: «A forfeit» (noun) is something you must give up or do as a punishment, often in a party game.
fact: The past tense of the verb is forfeited, as in «She forfeited her turn.»
exercise: «The team had to forfeit the match because they did not turn up.» What does forfeit mean here? | To play the match twice | *To lose the match because they did not play | To start the match early | To win the match easily
exercise: At the party, Sam had to pay a forfeit and do a silly dance. What is a forfeit here? | A prize for the winner | A song the band plays | *A silly task the loser must do | A kind of party food
exercise: «If you do not pay on time, you forfeit your place.» Which word is closest in meaning to forfeit? | Enjoy | Keep | *Lose | Gain
test: «Kai broke the rule, so he forfeited his turn.» What does forfeited mean? | Took two turns | Gave his turn to a friend for a prize | *Lost his turn because he broke the rule | Asked for a second chance
test: Which sentence uses forfeit as a noun? | She will forfeit her seat if she leaves | They forfeit points for cheating | *Every loser in the game had to pay a forfeit | The players must forfeit the game
exam: «The referee said the team would forfeit the match, because they broke the rules three times.» What does forfeit mean? | To win the match with a bonus point | To stop and rest for a while | To ask the referee to play again | *To lose the match because they broke the rules
